# The base Steam client prefix. Games get their own prefixes/profiles; this one
# exists to run the client itself (login, installs, updates).
#
# Reminder: never run two prefixes' Steam clients at once -- they share
# S:\steamapps and would fight over appmanifest state.

RUNTIME="wine-11.14-x86_64"
BACKEND="none"
PREFIX="steam-base"

EXE='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\Steam.exe'
WORKDIR="$PREFIXES_DIR/steam-base/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam"

ARGS=""

# Steam's UI is Chromium (steamwebhelper). Chromium's software compositor runs
# in the viz process and blits the rendered page into the browser process's
# window. Wine's window surfaces are per-process -- winemac.drv/surface.c hands
# a foreign hwnd a throwaway surface -- so those pixels are discarded and the
# window stays black.
#
# --in-process-gpu makes viz a thread of the browser process, so the blit lands
# in the window's real surface. CEF appends that switch by itself under
# CrossOver; ours does not, and there is no Steam option or registry key for it
# (see docs/NEXT.md). Steam restores its own binaries on launch, so a shim exe
# does not survive -- the injection lives in our Wine instead, via
# patches/wine-0004-kernelbase-append-args-env.patch.
PROFILE_ENV=(
    WINEDEBUG=-all
    'WINE_APPEND_ARGS=steamwebhelper.exe=--no-sandbox --in-process-gpu --disable-gpu'
)

# d3dcompiler_47 and corefonts are installed into the prefix by bin/mkprefix
# (winetricks), which also registers the native override in the prefix registry
# -- so nothing needs to be forced here any more.
#
# Deliberately NOT set: vulkan-1=n. Forcing it native breaks Steam's GPU
# topology query, which is what made the client fall back to a doomed GPU
# process in the first place.
WINEDLLOVERRIDES=""

# Deliberately NOT set: VK_ICD_FILENAMES. The Vulkan loader's default search
# finds MoltenVK correctly; pointing the variable at MoltenVK's own ICD is what
# hides it, because that manifest is flagged is_portability_driver. See
# docs/RUNTIME.md.
